examples/getting-started/hello-ui.ps1<pre><code># Hello, NativeHTMLKit.UI: a reactive counter in PowerShell.
#
# Teaches: New-NHKUi, New-NHKUiState, Add-NHKUiText -Bind, Add-NHKUiButton -Data/-OnClick,
#          Start-NHKUi and Stop-NHKUi.
# Run:     pwsh -File hello-ui.ps1        (Windows PowerShell 5.1: powershell.exe -File hello-ui.ps1)
# Guide:   docs/getting-started/powershell-ui.md
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
Import-Module NativeHTMLKit.UI -ErrorAction Stop   # also loads the NativeHTMLKit SDK
$app = Start-NativeHTMLKitScript -Name 'Counter'

$count = New-NHKUiState -Value 0
$label = New-NHKUiComputed -DependsOn @($count) -Data $count -Compute { param($c) "Count: $($c.Value)" }
$ui = New-NHKUi -Title 'Counter' -Theme cobalt -Density regular -Width 420 -Height 300
$null = Add-NHKUiColumn -UI $ui -Content {
    $null = Add-NHKUiHeading -UI $ui -Text 'Counter' -Level 1
    $null = Add-NHKUiText -UI $ui -Bind $label
    $null = Add-NHKUiRow -UI $ui -Content {
        $null = Add-NHKUiButton -UI $ui -Text '+1' -Data $count -OnClick { param($eventObject, $state) $state.Set([int]$state.Value + 1) }
        $null = Add-NHKUiButton -UI $ui -Text 'Reset' -Variant secondary -Data $count -OnClick { param($eventObject, $state) $state.Set(0) }
    }
}

try {
    $null = Start-NHKUi -UI $ui -Application $app   # opens the window and announces ready
    Wait-NativeHTMLKit -Application $app -UntilShutdown
} finally {
    Stop-NHKUi -UI $ui
    $label.Dispose()
    Close-NativeHTMLKit -Application $app
}
</code></pre>

examples/getting-started/hello.ps1<pre><code># Hello, NativeHTMLKit: your first native window from PowerShell.
#
# Teaches: Start-NativeHTMLKitScript, New-NativeHTMLKitWindow, Open-NativeHTMLKitHtml,
#          Register-NativeHTMLKitDocumentEvent, Set-NativeHTMLKitDocumentText, Wait-NativeHTMLKit.
# Run:     pwsh -File hello.ps1           (Windows PowerShell 5.1: powershell.exe -File hello.ps1)
# Guide:   docs/getting-started/powershell.md
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
Import-Module NativeHTMLKit -ErrorAction Stop
# Starts the native host, which runs this script again as its backend: keep side effects below.
$app = Start-NativeHTMLKitScript -Name 'Hello'

$page = @'
&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  body { font: 16px sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 32px; }
  button { padding: 8px 16px; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;Hello from PowerShell&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;button id="greet"&gt;Say hello&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;p id="status"&gt;Not clicked yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;
'@

try {
    $window = New-NativeHTMLKitWindow -Application $app -Title 'Hello' -Width 480 -Height 320
    $doc = Open-NativeHTMLKitHtml -Window $window -Html $page
    $counter = [pscustomobject]@{ Clicks = 0 }
    $null = Register-NativeHTMLKitDocumentEvent -Document $doc -Type click -Element greet -Callback {
        param($eventObject)
        $counter.Clicks++
        Set-NativeHTMLKitDocumentText -Document $doc -Element status -Text "Hello! You clicked $($counter.Clicks) time(s)."
    }
    Set-NativeHTMLKitReady -Application $app
    Wait-NativeHTMLKit -Application $app -UntilShutdown   # handle events until the window is closed
} finally {
    Close-NativeHTMLKit -Application $app
}
</code></pre>

examples/getting-started/hello.py<pre><code>"""Hello, NativeHTMLKit: your first native window from Python.

Teaches: Application.start(), open_html(), a click handler, set_text(), app.run().
Run:     python hello.py
Guide:   docs/getting-started/python.md
"""
from nativehtmlkit import Application

PAGE = """&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  body { font: 16px sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 32px; }
  button { padding: 8px 16px; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;Hello from Python&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;button id="greet"&gt;Say hello&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;p id="status"&gt;Not clicked yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"""


def main():
    # Application.start() starts the native host, which runs this script again as its backend.
    # Keep everything with side effects inside main(), after start().
    with Application.start(name="Hello") as app:
        window = app.open_html(PAGE, title="Hello", width=480, height=320)
        clicks = 0

        def greet(_event):
            nonlocal clicks
            clicks += 1
            window.document.set_text("status", f"Hello! You clicked {clicks} time(s).")

        window.document.on("click", greet, element="greet")
        app.run()  # announce "ready" and handle events until the window is closed


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
</code></pre>

examples/howto/python/clipboard_tool.py<pre><code>"""Clipboard text tool: paste text, transform it, copy the result back.

Teaches: Application.clipboard_text() and set_clipboard_text(), checking Application.capabilities()
for clipboard support, handling a failing clipboard request (RpcError) without crashing, and a &lt;form&gt; whose submit
applies the selected transformation.
Run:     python clipboard_tool.py
Guide:   docs/how-to/clipboard.md
"""
import json

from nativehtmlkit import Application, RpcError

PAGE = """&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  body { font: 14px sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 16px; background: #f4f6fa; color: #1d2433; }
  textarea { width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; height: 140px; font: 13px monospace; padding: 8px; }
  .bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; margin: 8px 0; }
  button, select { padding: 6px 10px; }
  #status { color: #5a6578; min-height: 1.2em; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;form id="tool"&gt;
    &lt;label for="input"&gt;Input&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;textarea id="input" placeholder="Paste or type text here"&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;
    &lt;div class="bar"&gt;
      &lt;button id="paste" type="button"&gt;Paste from clipboard&lt;/button&gt;
      &lt;select id="transform" aria-label="Transformation"&gt;
        &lt;option value="upper"&gt;UPPER CASE&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="lower"&gt;lower case&lt;/option&gt;
        &lt;option value="sort"&gt;Sort lines&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="unique"&gt;Remove duplicate lines&lt;/option&gt;
        &lt;option value="json"&gt;Pretty-print JSON&lt;/option&gt;
      &lt;/select&gt;
      &lt;button id="apply"&gt;Transform&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;label for="output"&gt;Result&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;textarea id="output" readonly&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;
    &lt;div class="bar"&gt;&lt;button id="copy" type="button"&gt;Copy result&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/form&gt;
  &lt;p id="status" role="status"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"""


def transform(kind, text):
    lines = text.splitlines()
    if kind == "upper":
        return text.upper()
    if kind == "lower":
        return text.lower()
    if kind == "sort":
        return "\n".join(sorted(lines, key=str.casefold))
    if kind == "unique":
        return "\n".join(dict.fromkeys(lines))
    if kind == "json":
        return json.dumps(json.loads(text), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)
    raise ValueError(kind)


def main():
    with Application.start(name="Clipboard tool") as app:
        window = app.open_html(PAGE, title="Clipboard tool", width=620, height=560)
        doc = window.document

        def apply(_event):
            try:
                result = transform(doc.get_value("transform"), doc.get_value("input"))
            except ValueError as error:  # json.JSONDecodeError is a ValueError
                doc.set_text("status", f"Cannot transform: {error}")
                return
            doc.set_value("output", result)
            doc.set_text("status", f"{len(result)} characters")

        def paste(_event):
            try:
                doc.set_value("input", app.clipboard_text())
                doc.set_text("status", "Pasted from the clipboard")
            except RpcError as error:  # for example code -32001 when this session has no clipboard
                doc.set_text("status", f"The clipboard is not available here ({error})")

        def copy(_event):
            try:
                app.set_clipboard_text(doc.get_value("output"))
                doc.set_text("status", "Copied the result to the clipboard")
            except RpcError as error:
                doc.set_text("status", f"The clipboard is not available here ({error})")

        # "available" is False when the host knows there is no clipboard (headless test mode) and
        # None on a desktop, where only the actual request can tell; so test for False explicitly.
        clipboard = app.capabilities().get("features", {}).get("clipboard_text", {})
        if clipboard.get("available") is False:
            for button in ("paste", "copy"):
                doc.set_attribute(button, "disabled", "")
            doc.set_text("status", "The clipboard is not available in this session; transformations still work.")

        doc.on("submit", apply, element="tool")
        doc.on("click", paste, element="paste")
        doc.on("click", copy, element="copy")
        app.run()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
</code></pre> <p>Real capture on KDE Plasma 6.6 Wayland with Core 1.0.3 and CLI 0.1.2.</p>

examples/howto/python/signup_form.py<pre><code>"""Sign-up form: native HTML form validation plus your own rules, then read the submitted values.

Teaches: required/type/minlength constraints checked by the host, set_custom_validity() for a rule
HTML cannot express (passwords must match), the "invalid" and "submit" events, validity(),
form_data() entries, reset_form(), and labelled controls that assistive technology can name.
Run:     python signup_form.py
Guide:   docs/how-to/forms.md
"""
from nativehtmlkit import Application

PAGE = """&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  body { font: 15px sans-serif; margin: 0; background: #f6f7fb; color: #1d2433; }
  main { max-width: 440px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px; }
  label { display: block; margin: 12px 0 4px; font-weight: 600; }
  input, select { width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #9aa6bf; border-radius: 6px; }
  input:invalid { border-color: #c0392b; }
  .check { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; margin-top: 12px; font-weight: normal; }
  .check input { width: auto; }
  button { margin-top: 16px; padding: 9px 16px; border: 0; border-radius: 6px; background: #2f6fd0; color: white; }
  #result { margin-top: 16px; padding: 12px; background: #e8f3ea; border-radius: 6px; }
  #result:empty { display: none; }
  #problem { color: #b03224; min-height: 1.2em; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;&lt;main&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;Create an account&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;form id="signup"&gt;
    &lt;label for="email"&gt;E-mail&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;input id="email" name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email"&gt;
    &lt;label for="password"&gt;Password (at least 8 characters)&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;input id="password" name="password" type="password" required minlength="8"&gt;
    &lt;label for="confirm"&gt;Repeat password&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;input id="confirm" name="confirm" type="password" required&gt;
    &lt;label for="plan"&gt;Plan&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;select id="plan" name="plan"&gt;&lt;option value="free"&gt;Free&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="team"&gt;Team&lt;/option&gt;&lt;/select&gt;
    &lt;label class="check"&gt;&lt;input id="terms" name="terms" type="checkbox" value="yes" required&gt; I accept the terms&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;button id="create"&gt;Create account&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/form&gt;
  &lt;p id="problem" role="alert"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;div id="result" role="status"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/main&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"""


def main():
    with Application.start(name="Sign up") as app:
        window = app.open_html(PAGE, title="Sign up", width=520, height=640)
        doc = window.document

        def passwords_changed(_event):
            # A custom validity message makes the field invalid until it is cleared again.
            same = doc.get_value("password") == doc.get_value("confirm")
            doc.set_custom_validity("confirm", "" if same else "The passwords do not match.")

        def invalid(event):
            # Sent once per failing control when a submit is attempted (it does not bubble). The host
            # focuses the first failing control, so report only that one.
            element = event.get("element")
            if (doc.focused_element() or {}).get("element") != element:
                return
            label = {"email": "E-mail", "password": "Password", "confirm": "Repeat password",
                     "terms": "Terms"}.get(element, "A field")
            doc.set_text("problem", f"{label}: {doc.validity(element)['message']}")

        def submitted(_event):
            # "submit" only arrives after every constraint (including the custom one) passed.
            entries = doc.form_data("signup")["entries"]
            values = {entry["name"]: entry["value"] for entry in entries}
            doc.set_text("problem", "")
            doc.set_text("result", f"Welcome, {values['email']}! Plan: {values['plan']}.")
            doc.reset_form("signup")

        doc.on("input", passwords_changed, element="password")
        doc.on("input", passwords_changed, element="confirm")
        doc.on("invalid", invalid)
        doc.on("submit", submitted, element="signup")
        doc.focus("email")
        app.run()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
</code></pre> <p>Real capture on KDE Plasma 6.6 Wayland with Core 1.0.3 and Python SDK 0.1.2.</p>

examples/howto/python/dialogs.py<pre><code>"""Project list with HTML dialogs: a confirmation dialog and a dialog that contains a form.

Teaches: show_dialog() (modal), close_dialog(element, return_value), reacting to the dialog's
"close" event and reading its return value with the "get_dialog" command (Escape closes a modal
dialog with an empty return value), and a &lt;form&gt; inside a dialog.
Run:     python dialogs.py
Guide:   docs/how-to/html-dialogs.md
"""
import html

from nativehtmlkit import Application

PAGE = """&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  body { font: 15px sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 20px; background: #f3f5f9; color: #1c2330; }
  li { margin: 6px 0; }
  button { padding: 6px 12px; margin-right: 6px; }
  dialog { border: 1px solid #9aa6bf; border-radius: 10px; padding: 20px; background: white; }
  dialog input { width: 260px; padding: 6px; }
  .danger { background: #c0392b; color: white; border: 0; border-radius: 5px; }
  #status { color: #5a6578; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;h1 id="heading"&gt;Projects&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;ul id="projects"&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
  &lt;button id="rename"&gt;Rename list...&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;button id="clear" class="danger"&gt;Delete all...&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;p id="status" role="status"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;dialog id="confirm" aria-labelledby="confirm-title"&gt;
    &lt;h2 id="confirm-title"&gt;Delete all projects?&lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This cannot be undone.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;button id="confirm-delete" class="danger"&gt;Delete&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;button id="confirm-cancel"&gt;Cancel&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/dialog&gt;

  &lt;dialog id="rename-dialog" aria-labelledby="rename-title"&gt;
    &lt;h2 id="rename-title"&gt;Rename the list&lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;form id="rename-form"&gt;
      &lt;input id="new-name" required maxlength="60" aria-label="New name"&gt;
      &lt;button id="rename-save"&gt;Save&lt;/button&gt;
      &lt;button id="rename-cancel" type="button"&gt;Cancel&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;/form&gt;
  &lt;/dialog&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"""


def main():
    with Application.start(name="Dialogs") as app:
        window = app.open_html(PAGE, title="Projects", width=560, height=520)
        doc = window.document
        projects = ["Website refresh", "Mobile app", "Data migration"]

        def render():
            doc.replace_html("projects", "".join(f"&lt;li&gt;{html.escape(p)}&lt;/li&gt;" for p in projects) or "&lt;li&gt;No projects&lt;/li&gt;")

        def confirm_closed(_event):
            # Every way of closing ends here: our buttons, or Escape (empty return value).
            choice = doc.command("get_dialog", element="confirm")["return_value"]
            if choice == "delete":
                projects.clear()
                render()
                doc.set_text("status", "All projects deleted")
            else:
                doc.set_text("status", "Nothing was deleted")

        def open_rename(_event):
            doc.set_value("new-name", doc.get_text("heading"))
            doc.show_dialog("rename-dialog")
            doc.focus("new-name")

        def rename_submitted(_event):
            doc.set_text("heading", doc.get_value("new-name").strip())  # set_text: the name is not HTML
            doc.close_dialog("rename-dialog", "saved")
            doc.set_text("status", "List renamed")

        doc.on("click", lambda _e: doc.show_dialog("confirm"), element="clear")
        doc.on("click", lambda _e: doc.close_dialog("confirm", "delete"), element="confirm-delete")
        doc.on("click", lambda _e: doc.close_dialog("confirm", "cancel"), element="confirm-cancel")
        doc.on("close", confirm_closed, element="confirm")
        doc.on("click", open_rename, element="rename")
        doc.on("submit", rename_submitted, element="rename-form")
        doc.on("click", lambda _e: doc.close_dialog("rename-dialog", "cancel"), element="rename-cancel")
        render()
        app.run()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
</code></pre> <p>Real capture on KDE Plasma 6.6 Wayland with Core 1.0.3 and Python SDK 0.1.2.</p> <ul> <li>One <code>close</code> handler decides for the confirmation dialog, whichever way it was closed.</li> <li>The rename dialog contains a form; Enter in the field submits it, and <code>required</code> stops an empty name.</li> <li>The new name is set with <code>set_text</code>, so it is never parsed as HTML.</li> </ul>

examples/howto/python/live_chart.py<pre><code>"""Live chart: draw a scrolling line chart into a live bitmap ten times per second.

Teaches: Document.create_bitmap() with &lt;img src="ui4me-bitmap://ID"&gt;, building straight-alpha
RGBA8 frames in Python, LiveBitmap.present() from a worker thread, a "change" event to pause,
labels in HTML next to the image, and closing the bitmap when the app ends.
Run:     python live_chart.py
Guide:   docs/how-to/live-bitmap-charts.md
"""
import math
import random
import threading
import time
from collections import deque

from nativehtmlkit import Application

WIDTH, HEIGHT = 400, 160
BACKGROUND = bytes((16, 22, 32, 255))
GRID = bytes((40, 52, 70, 255))
LINE = bytes((90, 170, 255, 255))

PAGE = """&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  body { font: 14px sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 16px; background: #0c1018; color: #dfe6f0; }
  img { display: block; border: 1px solid #2c3a50; border-radius: 6px; }
  .bar { display: flex; gap: 16px; align-items: center; margin-top: 10px; }
  #value { font: 600 22px monospace; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;Requests per second&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;img id="chart" src="ui4me-bitmap://requests" width="400" height="160" alt="Line chart of requests per second"&gt;
  &lt;div class="bar"&gt;
    &lt;span id="value" aria-live="polite"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;label&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="paused"&gt; Pause&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;span id="frames"&gt;0 frames&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"""


def base_frame():
    """Background with horizontal grid lines every 40 pixels."""
    frame = bytearray(BACKGROUND * (WIDTH * HEIGHT))
    for y in range(0, HEIGHT, 40):
        start = y * WIDTH * 4
        frame[start:start + WIDTH * 4] = GRID * WIDTH
    return bytes(frame)


def draw(base, samples, top):
    """Copy the background and draw the samples (newest on the right) as a connected line."""
    frame = bytearray(base)
    previous = None
    offset = WIDTH - len(samples)
    for i, value in enumerate(samples):
        x = offset + i
        y = HEIGHT - 1 - int(min(value, top) / top * (HEIGHT - 1))
        low, high = (y, y) if previous is None else (min(y, previous), max(y, previous))
        for row in range(low, high + 1):  # a vertical span joins this point to the previous one
            index = (row * WIDTH + x) * 4
            frame[index:index + 4] = LINE
        previous = y
    return frame


def main():
    with Application.start(name="Live chart") as app:
        window = app.open_html(PAGE, title="Live chart", width=460, height=320)
        doc = window.document
        bitmap = doc.create_bitmap("requests", WIDTH, HEIGHT)
        paused = threading.Event()
        stopped = threading.Event()
        samples = deque(maxlen=WIDTH)
        base = base_frame()

        def run():
            frames, t = 0, 0.0
            while not stopped.wait(0.1):
                if paused.is_set():
                    continue
                t += 0.1
                value = 120 + 60 * math.sin(t / 2) + 25 * math.sin(t * 1.7) + random.uniform(-10, 10)
                samples.append(max(0.0, value))
                try:
                    bitmap.present(draw(base, samples, top=250))
                    frames += 1
                    doc.batch([{"op": "set_text", "element": "value", "text": f"{value:.0f} req/s"},
                               {"op": "set_text", "element": "frames", "text": f"{frames} frames"}])
                except Exception:
                    return  # the window closed or the app is shutting down: stop drawing

        def toggle(event):
            if event.get("checked"):
                paused.set()
            else:
                paused.clear()

        doc.on("change", toggle, element="paused")
        threading.Thread(target=run, name="chart", daemon=True).start()
        try:
            app.run()
        finally:
            stopped.set()
            bitmap.close()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
</code></pre> <p>Real capture on KDE Plasma 6.6 Wayland with Core 1.0.3 and Python SDK 0.1.2.</p> <ul> <li>The background with grid lines is computed once; each frame copies it and draws the line.</li> <li>Drawing and presenting run on a worker thread, ten frames per second; <code>stopped</code> ends the loop when the app shuts down.</li> </ul>

examples/howto/python/log_windows.py<pre><code>"""Log windows: open a viewer window per log source and keep track of them from the main window.

Teaches: app.open_html() for more windows, a separate Document per window, request_close(),
on_window_event() to notice a window that the user closed, and on_before_close() on the main
window to close the viewers along with it.
Run:     python log_windows.py
Guide:   docs/how-to/multiple-windows.md
"""
import html
import itertools

from nativehtmlkit import Application

SOURCES = {
    "web": ["GET / 200 12ms", "GET /login 200 9ms", "POST /login 302 41ms", "GET /admin 403 3ms"],
    "worker": ["job 41 started", "job 41 finished in 2.1s", "job 42 started", "job 42 failed: timeout"],
    "mail": ["queued 3 messages", "delivered &lt;alerts@example.org&gt;", "retrying 1 message"],
}

MAIN = """&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  body { font: 15px sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 20px; background: #f3f5f9; color: #1c2330; }
  form { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  select, button { padding: 6px 10px; }
  li { margin: 4px 0; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;Log sources&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;form id="open-form"&gt;
    &lt;select id="source" aria-label="Log source"&gt;%s&lt;/select&gt;
    &lt;button id="open"&gt;Open viewer&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/form&gt;
  &lt;h2&gt;Open viewers&lt;/h2&gt;
  &lt;ul id="viewers"&gt;&lt;li&gt;None&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"""

VIEWER = """&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  body { font: 13px monospace; margin: 0; padding: 14px; background: #101418; color: #d9e1ea; }
  h1 { font: 600 16px sans-serif; }
  button { font: 14px sans-serif; padding: 6px 10px; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;&lt;h1 id="title"&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ol id="lines"&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;button id="close"&gt;Close viewer&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"""


def main():
    with Application.start(name="Log windows") as app:
        options = "".join(f'&lt;option value="{k}"&gt;{k}&lt;/option&gt;' for k in SOURCES)
        main_window = app.open_html(MAIN % options, title="Log sources", width=480, height=420)
        doc = main_window.document
        viewers = {}  # window id -&gt; (window, label)
        numbers = itertools.count(1)

        def show_viewers():
            items = [f"&lt;li&gt;{html.escape(label)}&lt;/li&gt;" for _, label in viewers.values()]
            doc.replace_html("viewers", "".join(items) or "&lt;li&gt;None&lt;/li&gt;")

        def open_viewer(_event):
            source = doc.get_value("source")
            label = f"{source} #{next(numbers)}"
            viewer = app.open_html(VIEWER, title=f"Log: {label}", width=520, height=360)
            viewer.document.set_text("title", f"Log: {label}")
            viewer.document.replace_html("lines", "".join(f"&lt;li&gt;{html.escape(line)}&lt;/li&gt;" for line in SOURCES[source]))
            # Each window has its own document; this handler belongs to the viewer's document.
            viewer.document.on("click", lambda _e: viewer.request_close(), element="close")
            viewers[viewer.id] = (viewer, label)
            show_viewers()

        def window_event(params):
            # The SDK has already retired a closed window; drop it from our list too.
            if params["type"] == "closed" and viewers.pop(params["window_id"], None) and not main_window.closed:
                show_viewers()

        def closing_main():
            for viewer, _ in list(viewers.values()):
                if not viewer.closed:
                    viewer.request_close()
            return True  # allow the main window to close

        doc.on("submit", open_viewer, element="open-form")
        app.on_window_event(window_event)
        main_window.on_before_close(closing_main)
        app.run()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
</code></pre> <p>Real capture on KDE Plasma 6.6 Wayland with Core 1.0.3 and Python SDK 0.1.2.</p> <ul> <li>The viewer's Close button is handled on the viewer's document.</li> <li><code>window_event</code> removes a viewer from the list when the user closes it with the window's own close button.</li> <li><code>on_before_close</code> on the main window closes the viewers too, then allows the main window to close, which ends the application.</li> </ul>

examples/howto/python/theme_switcher.py<pre><code>"""Theme switcher: light/dark mode and accent colours with CSS custom properties.

Teaches: CSS custom properties (var()), @media (prefers-color-scheme) driven by the desktop or
overridden with Document.set_environment(), add_stylesheet() + replace_stylesheet() to swap one
small stylesheet at run time, and computed_style() to read back what the renderer resolved.
Run:     python theme_switcher.py
Guide:   docs/how-to/styling.md
"""
from nativehtmlkit import Application

PAGE = """&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  :root { --bg: #f5f7fb; --panel: #ffffff; --text: #1b2230; --muted: #5d6879; --accent: #2f6fd0; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root { --bg: #10151e; --panel: #19212e; --text: #e4e9f1; --muted: #9aa7ba; }
  }
  body { margin: 0; padding: 20px; font: 15px sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); }
  .panel { background: var(--panel); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 15%, transparent); }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .accent { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
  button.primary { background: var(--accent); color: white; border: 0; border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px 14px; }
  form { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 8px 12px; align-items: center; margin-top: 12px; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;div class="panel" id="panel"&gt;
    &lt;h1&gt;Appearance&lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;p class="muted"&gt;The page uses CSS variables; switching a theme changes a few of them.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;form id="appearance"&gt;
      &lt;label for="scheme"&gt;Colour scheme&lt;/label&gt;
      &lt;select id="scheme"&gt;&lt;option value="system"&gt;Follow the desktop&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="light"&gt;Light&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="dark"&gt;Dark&lt;/option&gt;&lt;/select&gt;
      &lt;label for="accent"&gt;Accent&lt;/label&gt;
      &lt;select id="accent"&gt;&lt;option value="#2f6fd0"&gt;Blue&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="#1f8a4c"&gt;Green&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="#b4451f"&gt;Orange&lt;/option&gt;&lt;/select&gt;
      &lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;button class="primary" id="apply"&gt;Apply&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;/form&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Resolved accent: &lt;span class="accent" id="resolved"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"""


def main():
    with Application.start(name="Theme switcher") as app:
        window = app.open_html(PAGE, title="Theme switcher", width=520, height=420)
        doc = window.document
        # A separate, replaceable stylesheet for the run-time accent colour.
        accent_sheet = doc.add_stylesheet(":root { --accent: #2f6fd0; }")["sheet"]

        def show_resolved():
            style = doc.computed_style(["color"], "resolved")
            doc.set_text("resolved", style["properties"]["color"]["value"])

        def apply(_event):
            # "light"/"dark" override the desktop preference for this document; "system" follows it again.
            doc.set_environment(color_scheme=doc.get_value("scheme"))
            accent = doc.get_value("accent")
            if accent.startswith("#") and len(accent) == 7:  # only values from our own &lt;select&gt;
                doc.replace_stylesheet(accent_sheet, f":root {{ --accent: {accent}; }}")
            show_resolved()

        doc.on("submit", apply, element="appearance")
        show_resolved()
        app.run()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
</code></pre> <ul> <li>Define colours as custom properties on <code>:root</code>, and override them for <code>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)</code>.</li> <li><code>set_environment(color_scheme="light" | "dark" | "system")</code> overrides the desktop preference for one document (<code>reduced_motion="reduce" | "no-preference" | "system"</code> works the same way). PowerShell: <code>Set-NativeHTMLKitEnvironment</code>.</li> <li><code>add_stylesheet(css)</code> returns a sheet handle; <code>replace_stylesheet(sheet, css)</code> swaps its rules; <code>remove_stylesheet(sheet)</code> drops it. PowerShell: <code>Add-NativeHTMLKitStylesheet</code>, <code>Set-NativeHTMLKitStylesheet [-Remove]</code>.</li> <li><code>computed_style([properties], element)</code> reports the resolved values and whether each property is supported.</li> </ul>

examples/howto/python/status_board.py<pre><code>"""Status board: change parts of a live page without reloading it.

Teaches: set_text() for untrusted text, set_attribute(), add_class()/remove_class(),
batch() to apply several changes as one transaction, query() to find elements by CSS selector,
remove(), and insert_html() with escaped values.
Run:     python status_board.py
Guide:   docs/how-to/update-the-page.md
"""
import html
import itertools
import time

from nativehtmlkit import Application

SERVICES = {"api": "Public API", "web": "Web shop", "mail": "Mail relay"}
STATES = ("ok", "degraded", "down")

PAGE = """&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  body { font: 15px sans-serif; margin: 0; background: #f3f5f9; color: #1c2330; }
  main { padding: 20px; max-width: 640px; }
  .service { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; background: white;
             border: 1px solid #d6dce8; border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 14px; margin: 6px 0; }
  .pill { border-radius: 999px; padding: 2px 10px; font-size: 13px; background: #dfe6f1; }
  .ok .pill { background: #d5f0dc; color: #1d6b34; }
  .degraded .pill { background: #fbecc8; color: #7a5300; }
  .down .pill { background: #f8d6d6; color: #8a1f1f; }
  .note { color: #5a6578; font-size: 13px; }
  form { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 14px 0; }
  input, select, button { padding: 6px 8px; }
  #history li { font-size: 13px; color: #5a6578; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;&lt;main&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;Service status&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;div id="services"&gt;%(services)s&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;form id="update"&gt;
    &lt;select id="service" aria-label="Service"&gt;%(service_options)s&lt;/select&gt;
    &lt;select id="state" aria-label="Status"&gt;%(state_options)s&lt;/select&gt;
    &lt;input id="note" placeholder="Note (optional)" aria-label="Note" maxlength="120"&gt;
    &lt;button id="apply"&gt;Update&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;button id="clear" type="button"&gt;Clear history&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/form&gt;
  &lt;h2&gt;History&lt;/h2&gt;
  &lt;ul id="history"&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/main&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"""


def build_page():
    services = "".join(
        f'&lt;div class="service ok" id="svc-{key}"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;{html.escape(name)}&lt;/strong&gt;'
        f'&lt;div class="note" id="note-{key}"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span class="pill" id="pill-{key}"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;'
        for key, name in SERVICES.items())
    return PAGE % {
        "services": services,
        "service_options": "".join(f'&lt;option value="{k}"&gt;{html.escape(v)}&lt;/option&gt;' for k, v in SERVICES.items()),
        "state_options": "".join(f"&lt;option&gt;{s}&lt;/option&gt;" for s in STATES),
    }


def main():
    with Application.start(name="Status board") as app:
        window = app.open_html(build_page(), title="Status board", width=700, height=640)
        doc = window.document
        entry_ids = itertools.count(1)

        def update(_event):
            key, state = doc.get_value("service"), doc.get_value("state")
            note = doc.get_value("note").strip()
            # One atomic transaction: the page never shows a half-updated row.
            operations = [{"op": "remove_class", "element": f"svc-{key}", "name": s} for s in STATES]
            operations += [
                {"op": "add_class", "element": f"svc-{key}", "name": state},
                {"op": "set_text", "element": f"pill-{key}", "text": state},
                {"op": "set_text", "element": f"note-{key}", "text": note},  # text, never parsed as HTML
                {"op": "set_attribute", "element": f"svc-{key}", "name": "title",
                 "value": f"Changed {time.strftime('%H:%M:%S')}"},
            ]
            doc.batch(operations)
            entry = f"{time.strftime('%H:%M:%S')} {SERVICES[key]}: {state}" + (f" ({note})" if note else "")
            doc.insert_html("history", f'&lt;li id="h-{next(entry_ids)}"&gt;{html.escape(entry)}&lt;/li&gt;', position="afterbegin")
            doc.set_value("note", "")

        def clear(_event):
            for element in doc.query("#history li")["ids"]:
                doc.remove(element)

        doc.on("submit", update, element="update")
        doc.on("click", clear, element="clear")
        app.run()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
</code></pre> <p>Real capture on KDE Plasma 6.6 Wayland with Core 1.0.3 and Python SDK 0.1.2.</p> <ul> <li><code>batch()</code> applies all operations atomically: the user never sees a row with the new class but the old label. An invalid operation rejects the whole batch.</li> <li>The note comes from the user, so it is set with a <code>set_text</code> operation; the history entry is built as HTML, so the text is escaped first.</li> <li><code>query("#history li")</code> returns the ids of matching elements (elements without an id are counted but not listed; use <code>query_nodes</code> for those).</li> </ul>

examples/tutorials/powershell-process-dashboard/step1-snapshot.ps1<pre><code># Process dashboard tutorial, step 1: show a table of the busiest processes in a native window.
#
# Teaches: Start-NativeHTMLKitScript, New-NativeHTMLKitWindow, Open-NativeHTMLKitHtml, building
#          HTML rows from objects with HtmlEncode, Set-NativeHTMLKitDocumentHtml, Wait-NativeHTMLKit.
# Run:     pwsh -File step1-snapshot.ps1      (Windows PowerShell 5.1: powershell.exe -File step1-snapshot.ps1)
# Guide:   docs/tutorials/powershell-process-dashboard.md (step 1 of 3)
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
Import-Module NativeHTMLKit -ErrorAction Stop
# The host runs this script again as its backend: everything below this line runs in that backend.
$app = Start-NativeHTMLKitScript -Name 'Process Dashboard'

$page = @'
&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  body { font: 14px sans-serif; margin: 0; background: #11161f; color: #e6ebf3; }
  main { padding: 18px 22px; }
  h1 { font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #2a3445; }
  th { color: #9fb0c8; font-weight: 600; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;&lt;main&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;Top processes by memory&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;table&gt;
    &lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Name&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th class="num"&gt;Id&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th class="num"&gt;Memory (MB)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th class="num"&gt;CPU (s)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
    &lt;tbody id="rows"&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;
  &lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/main&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;
'@

function ConvertTo-HtmlText([string]$Text) { return [System.Net.WebUtility]::HtmlEncode($Text) }

function Get-ProcessRowsHtml([int]$Top) {
    $rows = Get-Process | Sort-Object WorkingSet64 -Descending | Select-Object -First $Top | ForEach-Object {
        '&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;{0}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td class="num"&gt;{1}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td class="num"&gt;{2:N1}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td class="num"&gt;{3:N1}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;' -f `
            (ConvertTo-HtmlText $_.ProcessName), $_.Id, ($_.WorkingSet64 / 1MB), [double]$_.CPU
    }
    return ($rows -join '')
}

try {
    $window = New-NativeHTMLKitWindow -Application $app -Title 'Process Dashboard' -Width 720 -Height 560
    $doc = Open-NativeHTMLKitHtml -Window $window -Html $page
    Set-NativeHTMLKitDocumentHtml -Document $doc -Element rows -Html (Get-ProcessRowsHtml -Top 15)
    Set-NativeHTMLKitReady -Application $app
    Wait-NativeHTMLKit -Application $app -UntilShutdown
} finally {
    Close-NativeHTMLKit -Application $app
}
</code></pre> <p>Run <code>pwsh -File step1-snapshot.ps1</code>.</p> <ul> <li>The page lives in a single-quoted here-string (<code>@' ... '@</code>), so PowerShell does not expand <code>$</code> or backticks inside the HTML.</li> <li><code>Get-ProcessRowsHtml</code> builds <code>&lt;tr&gt;</code> rows with the <code>-f</code> format operator. Process names are not under your control, so each one goes through <code>[System.Net.WebUtility]::HtmlEncode</code> before it becomes markup.</li> <li><code>Set-NativeHTMLKitDocumentHtml -Element rows</code> replaces the children of <code>&lt;tbody id="rows"&gt;</code>.</li> <li><code>Set-NativeHTMLKitReady</code> comes after the first content is in place, so the window opens with a filled table.</li> </ul>

examples/tutorials/powershell-process-dashboard/step2-filter.ps1<pre><code># Process dashboard tutorial, step 2: filter and sort the table.
#
# Teaches: Register-NativeHTMLKitDocumentEvent for "input" and "submit" events, reading controls with
#          Get-NativeHTMLKitValue, keeping view state in one object that callbacks can change,
#          Set-NativeHTMLKitDocumentText for untrusted text.
# Run:     pwsh -File step2-filter.ps1        (Windows PowerShell 5.1: powershell.exe -File step2-filter.ps1)
# Guide:   docs/tutorials/powershell-process-dashboard.md (step 2 of 3)
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
Import-Module NativeHTMLKit -ErrorAction Stop
$app = Start-NativeHTMLKitScript -Name 'Process Dashboard'

$page = @'
&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;style&gt;
  body { font: 14px sans-serif; margin: 0; background: #11161f; color: #e6ebf3; }
  main { padding: 18px 22px; }
  h1 { font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  form { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  input, select { background: #1b2331; color: #e6ebf3; border: 1px solid #3a475c; border-radius: 5px; padding: 6px; }
  #filter { flex: 1; }
  button { background: #3574c6; color: white; border: 0; border-radius: 5px; padding: 6px 12px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #2a3445; }
  th { color: #9fb0c8; font-weight: 600; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; }
  #summary { color: #9fb0c8; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;&lt;main&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;Processes&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;form id="view-form"&gt;
    &lt;input id="filter" type="search" placeholder="Filter by name" aria-label="Filter by name"&gt;
    &lt;select id="sort" aria-label="Sort by"&gt;
      &lt;option value="memory"&gt;Memory&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="cpu"&gt;CPU time&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="name"&gt;Name&lt;/option&gt;
    &lt;/select&gt;
    &lt;button id="apply"&gt;Refresh&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/form&gt;
  &lt;p id="summary"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;table&gt;
    &lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Name&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th class="num"&gt;Id&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th class="num"&gt;Memory (MB)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th class="num"&gt;CPU (s)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
    &lt;tbody id="rows"&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;
  &lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/main&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;
'@

function ConvertTo-HtmlText([string]$Text) { return [System.Net.WebUtility]::HtmlEncode($Text) }

function Update-View {
    $filter = (Get-NativeHTMLKitValue -Document $doc -Element filter).Trim()
    $sort = Get-NativeHTMLKitValue -Document $doc -Element sort
    $all = @(Get-Process)
    $shown = @($all | Where-Object { $filter -eq '' -or $_.ProcessName.IndexOf($filter, [StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase) -ge 0 })
    $sorted = switch ($sort) {
        'cpu'  { $shown | Sort-Object { [double]$_.CPU } -Descending }
        'name' { $shown | Sort-Object ProcessName }
        default { $shown | Sort-Object WorkingSet64 -Descending }
    }
    $html = @($sorted | Select-Object -First 25 | ForEach-Object {
        '&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;{0}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td class="num"&gt;{1}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td class="num"&gt;{2:N1}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td class="num"&gt;{3:N1}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;' -f `
            (ConvertTo-HtmlText $_.ProcessName), $_.Id, ($_.WorkingSet64 / 1MB), [double]$_.CPU
    }) -join ''
    Set-NativeHTMLKitDocumentHtml -Document $doc -Element rows -Html $html
    Set-NativeHTMLKitDocumentText -Document $doc -Element summary -Text ("Showing {0} of {1} processes" -f [Math]::Min(25, $shown.Count), $all.Count)
}

try {
    $window = New-NativeHTMLKitWindow -Application $app -Title 'Process Dashboard' -Width 720 -Height 600
    $doc = Open-NativeHTMLKitHtml -Window $window -Html $page
    # Callbacks run later, inside Wait-NativeHTMLKit, and can call the functions defined above.
    $null = Register-NativeHTMLKitDocumentEvent -Document $doc -Type input -Element filter -Callback { param($eventObject) Update-View }
    $null = Register-NativeHTMLKitDocumentEvent -Document $doc -Type change -Element sort -Callback { param($eventObject) Update-View }
    $null = Register-NativeHTMLKitDocumentEvent -Document $doc -Type submit -Element 'view-form' -Callback { param($eventObject) Update-View }
    Update-View
    Set-NativeHTMLKitReady -Application $app
    Wait-NativeHTMLKit -Application $app -UntilShutdown
} finally {
    Close-NativeHTMLKit -Application $app
}
</code></pre> <ul> <li>Three subscriptions call the same <code>Update-View</code> function: <code>input</code> on the search field (every keystroke), <code>change</code> on the sort <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>, and <code>submit</code> on the form (Enter or the Refresh button).</li> <li>Callbacks run later, inside <code>Wait-NativeHTMLKit</code>, and can call functions and read variables (<code>$doc</code>) defined in the script.</li> <li>The filter uses <code>IndexOf(..., OrdinalIgnoreCase)</code> rather than <code>-like "*$filter*"</code>, so characters like <code>[</code> typed by the user are not treated as wildcards.</li> <li><code>Set-NativeHTMLKitDocumentText</code> for the summary: text is never parsed as HTML.</li> </ul>

examples/tutorials/powershell-ui-settings/settings.ps1<pre><code># Settings editor: edit, validate and save a JSON settings file with NativeHTMLKit.UI (tutorial final code).
#
# Teaches: loading initial state from a file, computed validation and "unsaved changes" states,
#          buttons with -Data, saving JSON atomically, Revert, an Add-NHKUiAlert status line, and
#          starting the UI in the theme the user saved.
# Run:     pwsh -File settings.ps1 [-Path settings.json]
#          (Windows PowerShell 5.1: powershell.exe -File settings.ps1; default file:
#          nativehtmlkit-settings.json in your application-data folder)
# Guide:   docs/tutorials/powershell-ui-settings.md (step 2 of 2)
param([string]$Path)
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
Import-Module NativeHTMLKit.UI -ErrorAction Stop
$app = Start-NativeHTMLKitScript -Name 'Settings'

if (-not $Path) { $Path = Join-Path ([Environment]::GetFolderPath([Environment+SpecialFolder]::ApplicationData, [Environment+SpecialFolderOption]::Create)) 'nativehtmlkit-settings.json' }
$Path = [IO.Path]::GetFullPath($Path)
$defaults = [ordered]@{ DisplayName = ''; Email = ''; Theme = 'cobalt'; RefreshSeconds = 60; Notifications = $false }
$themes = @('cobalt', 'graphite', 'daylight')

function Read-Settings {
    $result = [ordered]@{}
    foreach ($key in $defaults.Keys) { $result[$key] = $defaults[$key] }
    if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $Path -PathType Leaf) {
        $data = [IO.File]::ReadAllText($Path) | ConvertFrom-Json
        foreach ($key in $defaults.Keys) {
            if ($null -ne $data.PSObject.Properties[$key]) { $result[$key] = $data.$key }
        }
    }
    if ($themes -notcontains $result.Theme) { $result.Theme = 'cobalt' }
    return $result
}

function Get-Snapshot {
    # The values as they would be saved; also used to detect unsaved changes.
    return [ordered]@{ DisplayName = $name.Value.Trim(); Email = $email.Value.Trim(); Theme = $theme.Value
        RefreshSeconds = $interval.Value.Trim(); Notifications = [bool]$notify.Value }
}

function Save-Settings {
    $snapshot = Get-Snapshot
    $snapshot.RefreshSeconds = [int]$snapshot.RefreshSeconds
    $json = ConvertTo-Json -InputObject $snapshot
    $folder = [IO.Path]::GetDirectoryName($Path)
    if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $folder)) { $null = New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $folder }
    $temporary = Join-Path $folder ('.settings-' + [guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N') + '.tmp')
    [IO.File]::WriteAllText($temporary, $json, (New-Object Text.UTF8Encoding($false)))
    if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $Path) { [IO.File]::Replace($temporary, $Path, [NullString]::Value) } else { [IO.File]::Move($temporary, $Path) }
}

$loaded = Read-Settings
$name = New-NHKUiState -Value ([string]$loaded.DisplayName)
$email = New-NHKUiState -Value ([string]$loaded.Email)
$theme = New-NHKUiState -Value ([string]$loaded.Theme)
$interval = New-NHKUiState -Value ([string]$loaded.RefreshSeconds)
$notify = New-NHKUiState -Value ([bool]$loaded.Notifications)
$saved = New-NHKUiState -Value (ConvertTo-Json -InputObject (Get-Snapshot) -Compress)
$status = New-NHKUiState -Value "Editing $Path"
$all = @($name, $email, $theme, $interval, $notify, $saved)

$problem = New-NHKUiComputed -DependsOn $all -Compute {
    $s = Get-Snapshot
    $seconds = 0
    if ($s.DisplayName -eq '') { 'Enter a display name.' }
    elseif ($s.Email -notmatch '^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$') { 'The e-mail address looks invalid.' }
    elseif (-not [int]::TryParse($s.RefreshSeconds, [ref]$seconds) -or $seconds -lt 5 -or $seconds -gt 3600) { 'Refresh interval must be a whole number from 5 to 3600.' }
    else { '' }
}
$changes = New-NHKUiComputed -DependsOn $all -Compute {
    if ((ConvertTo-Json -InputObject (Get-Snapshot) -Compress) -eq $saved.Value) { 'All changes saved' } else { 'Unsaved changes' }
}
$hasProblem = New-NHKUiComputed -DependsOn @($problem) -Compute { $problem.Value -ne '' }

$ui = New-NHKUi -Title 'Settings' -Theme $loaded.Theme -Density regular -Width 600 -Height 640
$null = Add-NHKUiColumn -UI $ui -Content {
    $null = Add-NHKUiRow -UI $ui -Content {
        $null = Add-NHKUiHeading -UI $ui -Text 'Settings' -Level 1
        $null = Add-NHKUiBadge -UI $ui -Bind $changes
    }
    $null = Add-NHKUiCard -UI $ui -Content {
        $null = Add-NHKUiInput -UI $ui -Bind $name -Label 'Display name'
        $null = Add-NHKUiInput -UI $ui -Bind $email -Label 'E-mail' -Type email
        $null = Add-NHKUiInput -UI $ui -Bind $interval -Label 'Refresh interval (seconds)' -Type number
        $null = Add-NHKUiSelect -UI $ui -Bind $theme -Label 'Theme (applies on next start)' -Options @(
            @{ Value = 'cobalt'; Label = 'Cobalt' }, @{ Value = 'graphite'; Label = 'Graphite' }, @{ Value = 'daylight'; Label = 'Daylight' })
        $null = Add-NHKUiCheckbox -UI $ui -Bind $notify -Label 'Send me e-mail notifications'
    }
    $null = Add-NHKUiWhen -UI $ui -Bind $hasProblem -Content {
        $null = Add-NHKUiText -UI $ui -Bind $problem
    }
    $null = Add-NHKUiRow -UI $ui -Content {
        $null = Add-NHKUiButton -UI $ui -Text 'Save' -OnClick {
            param($eventObject, $data)
            if ($problem.Value -ne '') { $status.Set('Fix the problem above before saving.'); return }
            try {
                Save-Settings
                $saved.Set((ConvertTo-Json -InputObject (Get-Snapshot) -Compress))
                $status.Set("Saved $(Get-Date -Format 'HH:mm:ss')")
            } catch {
                $status.Set('Could not save: ' + $_.Exception.Message)
            }
        }
        $null = Add-NHKUiButton -UI $ui -Text 'Revert' -Variant secondary -OnClick {
            param($eventObject, $data)
            $fresh = Read-Settings
            $name.Set([string]$fresh.DisplayName); $email.Set([string]$fresh.Email); $theme.Set([string]$fresh.Theme)
            $interval.Set([string]$fresh.RefreshSeconds); $notify.Set([bool]$fresh.Notifications)
            $status.Set('Reverted to the saved file')
        }
    }
    $null = Add-NHKUiAlert -UI $ui -Bind $status
}

try {
    $null = Start-NHKUi -UI $ui -Application $app
    Wait-NativeHTMLKit -Application $app -UntilShutdown
} finally {
    Stop-NHKUi -UI $ui
    foreach ($c in @($problem, $changes, $hasProblem)) { $c.Dispose() }
    Close-NativeHTMLKit -Application $app
}
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>param([string]$Path)</code>: <code>pwsh -File settings.ps1 -Path ./my-settings.json</code>. Without it, the file is <code>nativehtmlkit-settings.json</code> in your application-data folder (<code>[Environment]::GetFolderPath(...ApplicationData, Create)</code>, which creates the folder if it is missing: <code>%APPDATA%</code> on Windows, <code>~/.config</code> on Linux).</li> <li><code>Read-Settings</code> starts from defaults and copies known keys from the file, so a partial or older file still works.</li> <li><code>Get-Snapshot</code> returns the values as they would be saved. Two computed values use it: <code>$problem</code> (a validation message or <code>''</code>) and <code>$changes</code>, which compares the snapshot with <code>$saved</code>, the JSON of the last saved state.</li> <li><code>$hasProblem</code> is computed from <code>$problem</code> and drives <code>Add-NHKUiWhen</code>, which shows the message only when there is one.</li> <li>Save refuses to write while there is a problem, writes a temporary file and replaces the real one (<code>[IO.File]::Replace</code>, with <code>[NullString]::Value</code> for "no backup", since a plain <code>$null</code> would be passed as an empty string), then updates <code>$saved</code>, so the badge returns to "All changes saved".</li> <li>Revert reads the file again and sets every state; the bound inputs update themselves.</li> <li><code>New-NHKUi -Theme $loaded.Theme</code>: the theme is chosen when the UI is built, so a changed theme applies on the next start.</li> <li>Button callbacks are script blocks defined in the script. They can call <code>Save-Settings</code> and read <code>$problem</code>, <code>$status</code> and the other states directly.</li> </ul>
